    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup today is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, whose 83.29 efficiency score makes him our clear standout play. Facing Jack Flaherty, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a strong park factor and a dynamic platoon advantage that elevates his base projection significantly. Similarly, **Josh Jung** (63.73) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (62.64) represent high-upside options; **Josh Jung** is boosted by a favorable matchup against the hittable Grayson Rodriguez, while **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** remains a must-start due to his elite xwOBA despite facing the challenge of a tough outing against Bubba Chandler. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** also projects as a reliable contributor (60.24) provided he maintains his projected #2 spot in the order.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the card involved **Andy Pages**, who narrowly missed the cut with a score of 45.29. While his lineup position and potential for production were notable, the optimizer ultimately pivoted away from him in favor of the defensive and speed utility offered by **Nasim Nunez** and **Gage Workman**, whose park factors and platoon splits provided a slightly higher floor for our scarcity-driven strategy. We are closely monitoring the status of **Kyle Tucker** (52.99) and **Josh Lowe** (48.71); both are facing Jacob deGrom or Logan Henderson\u2014elite arms that drag down their SP skill scores. While **Kyle Tucker** is too talented to bench, the deGrom matchup represents a high risk for **Josh Lowe**, who must navigate the combined threat of an elite arm and his own steal-suppressing status against high-tier pitching. \n\nManagement remains cautious regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" designations for **Dominic Smith** (59.96), **Jackson Merrill** (53.04), and **Coby Mayo** (49.83). While **Dominic Smith** is currently positioned for a strong day against Miles Mikolas, any late-scratch or order drop for these players could force a mid-day adjustment. We are holding **Nolan Schanuel**, **Miguel Vargas**, and **Sam Antonacci** in reserve; while **Sam Antonacci** possesses excellent underlying metrics, he is the odd man out in today's rotation due to the specific need for higher-scoring starters across the middle infield and outfield slots.",
